! CLEAR          No impurities added to glass mix
! LOW IRON       Clear glass with low iron content, resulting in higher transmittance
! TINT           Tinted with inorganic materials to increase absorption
! BRONZE, GREY, GREEN, BLUE: Tinted the indicated color
! REF            Reflective -- metallic coating on one surface to increase solar reflection.
!                REF A: stainless steel coating; REF B: titanium coating;
!                REF C: pewter coating; REF D: tin-oxide coating;
!                LO, MID, HI: low, medium and high transmittance coating, respectively.
! LoE            Low-emissivity metallic coating
! SPEC SEL       Spectrally selective: part of solar spectrum preferentially transmitted
! PYR            Pyrolytic coating
! COATED POLY-xx Coated polyester film with nominal visible transmittance of xx percent
! Rev            Reversed: Coating is on front side instead of back side
! ECABS          Electrochromic glass that darkens by becoming more absorptive
! ECREF          Electrochromic glass that darkens by becoming more reflective
! BLEACHED       Bleached (lightest) state of electrochromic glass
! COLORED        Colored (darkest) state of electrochromic glass
!
! The values after the name are:
!   Th:  Thickness (m)
!   Ts:  Solar Transmittance at Normal Incidence
!   Rfs: Front Side Solar Reflectance at Normal Incidence
!   Rbs: Back Side Solar Reflectance at Normal Incidence
!   Tv:  Visible Transmittance at Normal Incidence
!   Rfv: Front Side Visible Reflectance at Normal Incidence
!   Rbv: Back Side Visible Reflectance at Normal Incidence
!   Tir: Infrared Transmittance at Normal Incidence
!   Ef:  Front Side Infrared Hemispherical Emissivity
!   Eb:  Back Side Infrared Hemispherical Emissivity
!   Con: Conductivity {W/m-K}
! where
!   "Front" is side of glass furthest from zone window is defined in
!   "Back" is side of glass closest to zone window is defined in
!
! ID is the identification number in the WINDOW 4 glass library
!
! All solar and visible transmittance and reflectance values are spectral average values
!
!                    Name                                         Th   Ts   Rfs  Rbs  Tv   Rfv  Rbv Tir Ef  Eb Con
! The objects and syntax in this dataset comply with EnergyPlus, Version 8.4.0 and above, unless otherwise noted.

